## Context
`rules/zotero.md` (§ Periodic sync + purge) says to reconcile staging to Zotero
periodically. Until PR #1434, `/molt` step 1.8 did this on every `/lair`; that
step was removed because it fired in any repository with `docs/` and stalled
for minutes. Nothing now runs the reconcile on a schedule, so paper
repositories lose automatic drift detection.

Decision for the author: accept on-demand `/zotero reconcile` only and say so
in the rule, or name a trigger scoped to paper repositories (for example the
presence of `.zotero-reconcile.json`, or a step in a paper-repo skill).

## Decision (author, 2026-10-15, binding)
The periodic staging reconcile is PROPOSED at /lair, never run automatically.
Trigger: the project has a docs/ directory and some file under docs/ was added
or modified since the start of the current day (mtime; docs/ is git-ignored per
rules/zotero.md, so git cannot see it). Lair then proposes `/zotero reconcile`
in its report; the author accepts or not. No trigger: silent. Cheap: mtime scan,
no Zotero access, no network. Do not reintroduce molt step 1.8.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `rules/zotero.md` names who runs the reconcile and when, matching what the skills actually do
